planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
- Readers of .moe/daemon.json in moe-jetbrains:
  - readDaemonInfo, called from connect, connectWithRetry, ensureDaemonRunningImpl, restartDaemon and getDaemonInfo. getDaemonInfo backs the status popup on the EDT, which today can delete the file.
  - replacementMetadataCleared (RF03).
  - task-90664db1's rereadDaemonInfo.
  - MoeMessageDispatcher's STATE_SNAPSHOT check, which deletes (follow-up task-007c0ea8).
- Today's deleters:
  - readDaemonInfo, on a mismatch;
  - ensureDaemonRunningImpl, for a stale file;
  - connect(), for a stale file;
  - handleForeignDaemon, guarded;
  - restartDaemon, after the stop;
  - the STATE_SNAPSHOT check.
- DaemonIdentityProbe.comparableProjectPath (DaemonIdentity.kt, landed by task-90664db1) already maps D:\x, D:/x, /mnt/d/x, //wsl$/<distro>/x and \\wsl.localhost\<distro>\x to one form. Reuse it.
- The daemon's own rules (packages/moe-daemon/src/index.ts; see mem:gotcha-daemon-lifecycle-wsl-foreign):
  - isForeignDaemonInfo defines the other side;
  - validateDaemonInfoForProject;
  - existingDaemonBlocksStart cleans a same-side mismatch and proceeds, but blocks an other-side mismatch with exit 1 and never removes it;
  - stopDaemon sends no signal for an other-side file.
- Gson builds Kotlin data classes without calling their constructor, so an absent projectPath arrives as a runtime null in a non-null String. Today that reads as null through an exception; keep it so.
- The test helper supervisor(root, ...) leaves profile at its default. New rows that need LEGACY pass profile = { RuntimeProfile.LEGACY } explicitly, as the rows near lines 181, 202 and 220 do.
- Kotlin tests run from WSL through cmd.exe gradlew.bat, under the jetbrains-gradle lease.
